<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνορέη</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνορέα</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήρ</span>) poet. word for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρεία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>manhood, prowess</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνορέῃ πίσυνοι καὶ κάρτεϊ χειρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.226
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρτεΐ τε σθένεΐ τε πεποιθότας
					ἠνορέῃ τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.329
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποσύνῃ τε καὶ ἠνορέηφι πεποιθώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.303
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκῇ τ᾽ ἠνορέῃ τε κεκάσμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.509
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνορέας οὐκ ἀμπλακών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					8.67
				</span></i>
			; <i>manly beauty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. ἐρατεινήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.156
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατος ἠ</span>. its
				<i>strength</i>, Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				10.40
			</span></i>; <i>force</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλάκι τοι ῥέα μῦθος, ὅ κεν μόλις
					ἐξανύσειεν ἠνορέη, τόδ᾽ ἔρεξε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.189
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <i>triumphs of manhood</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.20
			</span></i>. (Perh. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνορία</span> with 
				Aeol.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρε-</span> fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρι-</span>.)</div>
